# "/diagnostics" once a language server is actually running. Gated by LSP_TEST because it
# needs gopls on PATH, which CI's lsp job provides and a plain `make test` does not.
#
# The server is started the way a user starts it: a file read. That path was dead until issue
# #111 — IsAvailable() gated the warmup whose purpose is to start the server — so this
# scenario is also the regression guard for that fix: if the circle returns, the warmup never
# runs, IsAvailable() stays false, and the status line says "LSP not available" instead of the
# literal asserted here.
#
# The assertion is "No LSP diagnostics." rather than a listing: this workspace has gopls with
# nothing to report, and that string is only reachable when a client exists. The listing (the
# third outcome) would need real diagnostics present.
# The wipe drops the write permission the language server needs before removing it: gopls
# resolves the workspace through the redirected HOME, so the previous run left a read-only
# Go module cache under $HOME/go/pkg/mod and `rm -rf` alone could not empty the directory.
# It then failed, the `&&` chain stopped, the stub never started, and the second run of this
# scenario died on "connection refused" instead of on anything LSP-related (issue #115).
open --dir . --size 120x30 --env HOME=/tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp --env TERM=xterm-256color --env COLORTERM=truecolor --env CLICOLOR_FORCE=1 --env NO_COLOR -- /bin/sh -c 'chmod -R u+w /tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp 2>/dev/null; rm -rf /tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp; mkdir -p /tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp/.tinycode /tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp/sessions && printf %s "{\"lsp\":{\"enabled\":true}}" > /tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp/.tinycode/config.json && python3 tui/testdata/stub/openai_stub.py 18511 read & sleep 1; ./bin/tinycode --base-url=http://127.0.0.1:18511/v1 --api-key=stub --model=stub --session-dir=/tmp/tinyscen-home-lsp/sessions --log-level=debug; status=$?; kill %1 2>/dev/null; exit $status'
wait --text "Get started" --timeout 20s
wait --text "Type your request" --timeout 20s
send --text "read main.go"
send --key enter
wait --text "read_file" --timeout 20s
send --text /diagnostics
send --key enter
wait --text "No LSP diagnostics." --timeout 30s
screenshot /tmp/tinyscen-shots/lsp-diagnostics-120x30.png --scale 2
send --text /exit
send --key enter
wait-exit 20s
expect-exit 0
